21ft|v|To clear (a liquid) from scum or substance floating or lying thereon, by means of a utensil that passes just beneath the surface; as, to skim milk; to skim broth. ; To take off by skimming; as, to skim cream. ; To pass near the surface of; to brush the surface of; to glide swiftly along the surface of. ; Fig.: To read or examine superficially and rapidly, in order to cull the principal facts or thoughts; as, to skim a book or a newspaper. ; To pass lightly; to glide along in an even, smooth course; to glide along near the surface. ; To hasten along with superficial attention. ; To put on the finishing coat of plaster.	d:1t1g,61,11;17nk,34,52;28oo,14,11~17nk,34,52;1t1g,61,11;28oo,14,11
